WEBVTT

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:02.320
In the source demo, the expert

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:04.620
demonstrates the best practice, explicitly

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:06.500
asking the agent to show its

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.920
work. Like in math class.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.420
Exactly. They prompt the agent to

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.400
use the governed revenue metric located

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.720
in the sales report semantic model,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.000
summarize it by store for a

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.780
specific time period, explicitly identify

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.720
the source measure it used, and

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.520
actually display the underlying query

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.360
code it executed.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:26.320
So you force the chat interface

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:28.660
to show you the exact DAX

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:29.820
or SQL code it wrote.

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:31.980
Yes. This gives the operator a

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:34.180
tangible mathematical calculation.

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:36.040
The operator can then take that

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.480
DAX code and compare it against

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.780
their traditional legacy power BI dashboard

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.339
using the exact same filters.
